# Template. Copy the pieces you need into the real files described below.
# Every file mentioned here except this one is git-ignored.
#
# NAMING RULE — this matters more than anything else in this file:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_*   -> shipped inside the app on every phone. Public forever.
#   everything else -> stays on your computer, used by scripts only.
# Never give a real secret an EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix.
#
# WHICH FILE LOADS WHEN (verified with `npx expo config`):
#   .env               always loaded, in both modes
#   .env.development   loaded by `npm start` (Expo Go)        -> mesura-dev
#   .env.production    loaded by `expo export` / EAS builds   -> mesura-prod
# A mode file beats .env when both define the same name.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.development   <- Supabase project "mesura-dev"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env.production    <- Supabase project "mesura-prod"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same two names, production values. (Phase 10 also mirrors these into EAS,
# because git-ignored files are not uploaded to Expo's build servers.)

# The Supabase "service_role" key belongs in NEITHER file, and nowhere in this
# project. It bypasses every security policy. It lives only in Supabase's own
# server-side settings.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .env               <- secrets for your machine only, no EXPO_PUBLIC_ prefix
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A GitHub Personal Access Token, used only by `npm run push`.
# Create one at https://github.com/settings/tokens?type=beta
# Give it access to the "mesura" repository, with Contents: Read and write.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
